cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "US Multi-Party System: A Proportional-Representation Election Simulation"
message: "If you use this simulation or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Decker
    given-names: Brayden
repository-code: "https://github.com/braydeck/USMultiPartySystem"
url: "https://usmultiparty.com/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive simulation of US elections under proportional representation,
  built from 45,707 2024 Cooperative Election Study responses via polychoric EFA,
  DPGMM clustering, spatial ballot generation, and STV / IRV / Condorcet elections.
keywords:
  - proportional representation
  - single transferable vote
  - ranked choice voting
  - Condorcet
  - electoral reform
  - political science
license: GPL-3.0
date-released: "2026-06-18"
